WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.917 --> 00:00:08.319
&gt;&gt;&gt; A major announcement today

00:00:08.319 --> 00:00:10.554
from Nikki Haley.

00:00:10.688 --> 00:00:12.790
The 2024 Republican presidential

00:00:12.923 --> 00:00:14.792
field has its second candidate

00:00:14.925 --> 00:00:16.927
and its first woman.

00:00:17.061 --> 00:00:19.296
&gt;&gt; The socialist left sees an

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:21.732
opportunity to rewrite history.

00:00:21.866 --> 00:00:23.901
China and Russia are on the

00:00:24.335 --> 00:00:25.335
March.

00:00:24.335 --> 00:00:26.337
They all think we can be

00:00:26.337 --> 00:00:27.037
bullied.

00:00:27.171 --> 00:00:27.671
Kicked around.

00:00:27.805 --> 00:00:30.341
You should know this about me.

00:00:30.474 --> 00:00:32.576
I don't put up with bullies, and

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:34.345
when you kick back, it hurts

00:00:34.345 --> 00:00:35.946
them more when you're wearing

00:00:36.347 --> 00:00:36.380
heels.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:39.350
I'm Nikki Haley, and I'm running

00:00:39.483 --> 00:00:40.017
for president.

00:00:40.351 --> 00:00:41.552
&gt;&gt; Tomorrow, the former south

00:00:41.685 --> 00:00:42.620
Carolina governor and ambassador

00:00:42.753 --> 00:00:44.655
to the united nations holds a

00:00:44.788 --> 00:00:46.357
kickoff rally in Charleston,

00:00:46.357 --> 00:00:47.691
then two other key early voting

00:00:47.825 --> 00:00:50.861
states, Iowa and New Hampshire,

00:00:50.995 --> 00:00:51.328
later this week.

00:00:51.462 --> 00:00:52.530
Joining now to share reporting

00:00:52.663 --> 00:00:56.367
and incites, Dana bash, Jeremy

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:58.002
diamond, and tia Mitchell.

00:00:58.369 --> 00:00:59.303
So Donald Trump has his first

00:00:59.436 --> 00:01:00.371
declared opponent.

00:01:00.371 --> 00:01:01.839
He was the only, until today,

00:01:01.972 --> 00:01:04.008
the only declared candidate for

00:01:04.375 --> 00:01:04.508
president.

00:01:04.508 --> 00:01:05.409
The question is, we roll back

00:01:05.543 --> 00:01:07.144
the tape pre-trump, you can make

00:01:07.278 --> 00:01:09.079
the case for okay, here's Nikki

00:01:09.213 --> 00:01:10.848
Haley.

00:01:10.981 --> 00:01:12.383
She's interesting, a governor of

00:01:12.483 --> 00:01:12.816
South Carolina.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:14.385
In the post trump Republican

00:01:14.385 --> 00:01:15.119
party, what's the lane?

00:01:15.252 --> 00:01:16.720
&gt;&gt; I was actually in south

00:01:16.854 --> 00:01:18.589
Carolina pre-trump when then

00:01:18.722 --> 00:01:20.791
governor Nikki Haley endorsed

00:01:20.925 --> 00:01:22.927
Marco Rubio and she stood on the

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:24.595
stage with Marco Rubio and Tim

00:01:24.728 --> 00:01:25.629
Scott and said this is what the

00:01:25.763 --> 00:01:27.298
new Republican party should look

00:01:27.431 --> 00:01:27.598
like.

00:01:27.731 --> 00:01:29.733
That was before she became

00:01:29.867 --> 00:01:30.467
Donald Trump's U.N. Ambassador

00:01:30.601 --> 00:01:32.403
and kind of went back and forth

00:01:32.403 --> 00:01:33.904
many times when it comes to

00:01:34.038 --> 00:01:35.039
supporting or not supporting

00:01:35.172 --> 00:01:35.306
him.

00:01:35.439 --> 00:01:36.640
That was one of the things that

00:01:36.774 --> 00:01:39.543
was most fascinating about her

00:01:39.677 --> 00:01:39.843
video.

00:01:39.977 --> 00:01:40.945
By the way, we could spend an

00:01:41.078 --> 00:01:42.413
hour talking about it,

00:01:42.546 --> 00:01:44.415
dissecting it, because it was

00:01:44.548 --> 00:01:47.017
very intentional.

00:01:47.151 --> 00:01:48.619
A lot of points she wanted to

00:01:48.752 --> 00:01:48.919
make.

00:01:49.053 --> 00:01:50.821
When you talk to people who are

00:01:50.955 --> 00:01:52.423
preparing to, thinking about

00:01:52.423 --> 00:01:53.190
running against Donald Trump,

00:01:53.324 --> 00:01:54.658
which is what it is right now,

00:01:54.792 --> 00:01:56.427
there seems to be a dividing

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:57.528
line between those who are

00:01:57.661 --> 00:02:00.497
willing to say, an aggressive

00:02:00.631 --> 00:02:02.433
full throated way, we have to

00:02:02.433 --> 00:02:06.437
move on beyond this man, Donald

00:02:06.437 --> 00:02:06.604
Trump.

00:02:06.737 --> 00:02:07.237
And those who are kind of

00:02:07.371 --> 00:02:07.738
dancing around it.

00:02:07.871 --> 00:02:09.540
I'm already hearing from some in

00:02:09.673 --> 00:02:11.241
the first camp saying okay, she

00:02:11.375 --> 00:02:13.177
talks about the heels, which is

00:02:13.644 --> 00:02:15.112
a great memorable line.

00:02:15.245 --> 00:02:16.847
She talks about bullies, which

00:02:16.981 --> 00:02:18.616
is another memorable line.

00:02:18.749 --> 00:02:21.585
But neglects to talk about her

00:02:21.719 --> 00:02:23.287
former boss who could easily be

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:24.455
put in that category.

00:02:24.555 --> 00:02:26.123
&gt;&gt; In fact, she kind of lumps

00:02:26.457 --> 00:02:26.924
him in.

00:02:27.057 --> 00:02:28.993
Not just Donald Trump, she says

00:02:29.126 --> 00:02:30.461
other Republican presidential

00:02:30.461 --> 00:02:33.864
candidates have failed a

00:02:33.998 --> 00:02:34.465
critical test.

00:02:34.498 --> 00:02:36.800
&gt;&gt; Republicans have lost the

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:38.636
popular vote in seven out of the

00:02:38.769 --> 00:02:40.537
last eight presidential

00:02:40.671 --> 00:02:40.904
elections.

00:02:41.038 --> 00:02:42.473
That has to change.

00:02:42.539 --> 00:02:44.475
It's time for a new generation

00:02:44.475 --> 00:02:45.943
of leadership.

00:02:46.076 --> 00:02:48.912
To rediscover fiscal

00:02:49.046 --> 00:02:50.147
responsibility, secure our

00:02:50.481 --> 00:02:51.849
border, and strengthen our

00:02:51.982 --> 00:02:54.985
country, our pride, and our

00:02:55.119 --> 00:02:55.619
purpose.

00:02:55.753 --> 00:02:58.656
&gt;&gt; It seemed to me to be a, if

00:02:58.789 --> 00:03:00.491
you're for trump or Desantis for

00:03:00.624 --> 00:03:02.493
that matter, if you're for a

00:03:02.493 --> 00:03:03.794
trumpy candidate, think again.

00:03:03.927 --> 00:03:05.863
Is that the point she's making,

00:03:05.996 --> 00:03:07.464
to shake the Republican primary

00:03:07.598 --> 00:03:08.499
voter, think again.

00:03:08.499 --> 00:03:10.501
&gt;&gt; I think she's saying that,

00:03:10.601 --> 00:03:12.136
but what is she giving them as a

00:03:12.503 --> 00:03:13.837
true kind of contrast to trump

00:03:13.971 --> 00:03:15.039
or Desantis?

00:03:15.172 --> 00:03:16.507
Because she's still talking

00:03:16.507 --> 00:03:18.509
about wokism and the radical

00:03:18.575 --> 00:03:20.778
left and criticizing the 1619

00:03:20.911 --> 00:03:21.478
project.

00:03:21.612 --> 00:03:23.113
These are all the same type of

00:03:23.247 --> 00:03:24.515
talking points you'll hear from

00:03:24.515 --> 00:03:26.517
a trump or a Desantis.

00:03:26.517 --> 00:03:28.519
So you know, to Dana's point,

00:03:28.519 --> 00:03:29.553
she's talking around the edges,

00:03:29.687 --> 00:03:32.122
not really saying the thing, and

00:03:32.523 --> 00:03:33.557
I don't know if that's going to

00:03:33.691 --> 00:03:35.092
resonate if she truly wants to

00:03:35.225 --> 00:03:40.531
present herself as an

00:03:40.531 --> 00:03:40.798
alternative.

00:03:40.931 --> 00:03:41.532
&gt;&gt; It's great question, does she

00:03:41.665 --> 00:03:43.667
run as governor Nikki Haley or

00:03:43.801 --> 00:03:44.668
ambassador Nikki Haley.

00:03:44.802 --> 00:03:46.170
Just look at the bio card.

00:03:46.537 --> 00:03:47.171
It's impressive.

00:03:47.304 --> 00:03:49.173
She's 51 years old.

00:03:49.306 --> 00:03:50.741
Joe Biden is 80 plus, Donald

00:03:50.874 --> 00:03:52.676
Trump would be 80 or 79.

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:53.377
51 years old.

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:54.812
First generation American.

00:03:54.945 --> 00:03:56.747
Was U.N. Ambassador.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:57.881
First woman South Carolina

00:03:58.015 --> 00:03:58.549
governor.

00:03:58.549 --> 00:04:00.084
She led the removal of the

00:04:00.217 --> 00:04:01.452
confederate flag from the south

00:04:01.585 --> 00:04:02.653
Carolina state house, that after

00:04:03.053 --> 00:04:04.722
a horrific shooting at a black

00:04:04.855 --> 00:04:05.055
church.

00:04:05.189 --> 00:04:06.790
Governor Nikki Haley would be an

00:04:06.924 --> 00:04:07.958
interesting Republican.

00:04:08.092 --> 00:04:09.893
Trump ambassador Nikki Haley,

00:04:10.027 --> 00:04:10.561
where's the lane?

00:04:10.594 --> 00:04:12.229
&gt;&gt; If you look at the video it's

00:04:12.563 --> 00:04:13.897
clear she plans on running as

00:04:14.031 --> 00:04:16.133
governor Nikki Haley, at least

00:04:16.567 --> 00:04:16.633
primarily.

00:04:16.633 --> 00:04:18.202
The entire video focuses on her

00:04:18.569 --> 00:04:19.603
time as governor, what she was

00:04:19.737 --> 00:04:21.805
able to do in the state from an

00:04:21.939 --> 00:04:25.275
economic perspective, how she

00:04:25.409 --> 00:04:27.244
handled the fallout of the

00:04:27.377 --> 00:04:27.978
devastating Charleston shooting.

00:04:28.112 --> 00:04:29.480
The only thing we see in the

00:04:29.613 --> 00:04:30.848
video in terms of U.N.

00:04:30.981 --> 00:04:32.216
Ambassador is maybe a picture or

00:04:32.583 --> 00:04:34.585
video of her in that role at the

00:04:34.685 --> 00:04:35.018
united nations.

00:04:35.152 --> 00:04:37.721
But I think the bigger question

00:04:37.855 --> 00:04:39.423
in terms of how she actually

00:04:39.556 --> 00:04:40.591
approaches this is we have seen

00:04:40.591 --> 00:04:42.593
too many of these Republicans

00:04:42.693 --> 00:04:44.595
kind of criticize trump

00:04:44.595 --> 00:04:45.462
obliquely but not actually want

00:04:45.596 --> 00:04:47.064
to do it directly.

00:04:47.197 --> 00:04:48.632
And she clearly seems to fall in

00:04:48.766 --> 00:04:49.466
that lane so far.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:50.934
When you look at her statements

00:04:51.068 --> 00:04:53.270
over just the last year, I mean,

00:04:53.403 --> 00:04:55.806
from January 6th insurrection,

00:04:55.939 --> 00:04:57.608
saying that trump let us down,

00:04:57.741 --> 00:04:59.176
we shouldn't have followed him,

00:04:59.309 --> 00:05:00.611
to then saying that she would

00:05:00.677 --> 00:05:02.679
not run if he ran, and that she

00:05:02.813 --> 00:05:03.947
would support him, to now

00:05:04.081 --> 00:05:04.748
running herself.

00:05:04.882 --> 00:05:07.084
It's not really clear where

00:05:07.217 --> 00:05:08.619
Nikki Haley actually stands and

00:05:08.619 --> 00:05:09.386
that's something she has to

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:10.087
focus on.

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:11.789
How does she define herself to

00:05:11.922 --> 00:05:13.223
these Republican primary voters.

00:05:13.357 --> 00:05:15.225
&gt;&gt; If you're watching at home

00:05:15.359 --> 00:05:16.627
saying why don't you care about

00:05:16.693 --> 00:05:18.629
what trump said about her or

00:05:18.695 --> 00:05:19.596
Pompeo said about her?

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:21.198
This is her announcement day.

00:05:21.331 --> 00:05:22.866
We focus on who they are and

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:23.901
what they want to do.

00:05:24.034 --> 00:05:25.235
But one of the key points she

00:05:25.369 --> 00:05:27.104
made here is she talked about

00:05:27.237 --> 00:05:27.437
it.

00:05:27.571 --> 00:05:28.806
She talked about being the

00:05:28.939 --> 00:05:31.208
daughter of immigrants in a

00:05:31.341 --> 00:05:31.842
state like South Carolina.

00:05:31.975 --> 00:05:33.477
She says it's defined her life.

00:05:33.610 --> 00:05:35.379
&gt;&gt; The railroad tracks divided

00:05:35.512 --> 00:05:37.848
the town by race.

00:05:38.015 --> 00:05:39.817
I was the proud daughter of

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:42.252
Indian immigrants.

00:05:42.653 --> 00:05:45.489
Not black, not white.

00:05:45.622 --> 00:05:46.657
I was different.

00:05:46.657 --> 00:05:47.758
But my mom would always say,

00:05:47.891 --> 00:05:51.161
your job is not to focus on the

00:05:51.295 --> 00:05:51.929
differences.

00:05:52.062 --> 00:05:54.264
But the similarities.

00:05:54.665 --> 00:05:56.667
&gt;&gt; Again, that part of her

00:05:56.667 --> 00:05:58.035
biography is compelling.

00:05:58.168 --> 00:05:59.503
Will she choose or will she try

00:05:59.636 --> 00:06:01.038
to be all things to all slices

00:06:01.171 --> 00:06:02.673
of the Republican primary?

00:06:02.706 --> 00:06:04.675
Because if she's a general

00:06:04.675 --> 00:06:06.910
election candidate, her team and

00:06:07.044 --> 00:06:09.012
her team argues we'll get back

00:06:09.146 --> 00:06:10.681
suburban women who can't vote

00:06:10.714 --> 00:06:12.683
for trump, we'll get back

00:06:12.683 --> 00:06:15.185
dependents looking for fiscal

00:06:15.319 --> 00:06:16.687
conservatives, maybe are pro

00:06:16.687 --> 00:06:18.021
life but don't want someone

00:06:18.155 --> 00:06:19.122
hitting them in the head with

00:06:19.256 --> 00:06:19.489
it.

00:06:19.623 --> 00:06:20.157
Where is her lane?

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:21.558
&gt;&gt; It's not where she's going

00:06:21.692 --> 00:06:22.893
right now, which I guess in a

00:06:23.026 --> 00:06:24.328
lot of ways is understandable

00:06:24.695 --> 00:06:25.562
because that's not the

00:06:25.696 --> 00:06:27.064
electorate she's appealing to,

00:06:27.197 --> 00:06:28.098
it's Republicans.

00:06:28.232 --> 00:06:29.700
The part right after what you

00:06:29.833 --> 00:06:33.237
played in the video, she talks

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:36.707
about the need to not talk about

00:06:36.707 --> 00:06:38.842
the differences so much and talk

00:06:38.976 --> 00:06:40.978
about similarities when it comes

00:06:41.111 --> 00:06:43.780
to race and other parts of

00:06:43.914 --> 00:06:44.114
America.

00:06:44.248 --> 00:06:46.383
She has an image of AOC looking

00:06:46.717 --> 00:06:48.719
angry, and she has another image

00:06:48.752 --> 00:06:50.721
of an African American woman.

00:06:50.988 --> 00:06:53.423
I thought that was absolutely

00:06:53.557 --> 00:06:54.358
fascinating because she is a

00:06:54.725 --> 00:06:55.559
woman of color.

00:06:55.692 --> 00:06:58.262
And she's trying to show that

00:06:58.395 --> 00:06:59.529
she's with the Republicans when

00:06:59.663 --> 00:07:02.900
it comes to the culture wars and

00:07:03.033 --> 00:07:05.135
everything that Ron Desantis and

00:07:05.269 --> 00:07:07.037
you name it have been talking

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:10.173
about when it comes to trying to

00:07:10.307 --> 00:07:12.342
exploit the differences on

00:07:12.743 --> 00:07:14.244
ethnicity and race as opposed to

00:07:14.378 --> 00:07:14.878
bringing them together.

00:07:15.012 --> 00:07:16.747
&gt;&gt; Here's the question I can't

00:07:16.847 --> 00:07:17.047
answer.

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:19.850
If you go back to earlier in our

00:07:19.983 --> 00:07:21.718
days, pre-trump days, she's a

00:07:21.852 --> 00:07:22.986
candidate very good in small

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:24.388
group settings like this.

00:07:24.755 --> 00:07:25.555
Meaning she could have great

00:07:25.689 --> 00:07:26.757
appeal in Iowa.

00:07:26.757 --> 00:07:27.524
Then her state, South Carolina,

00:07:27.658 --> 00:07:28.759
is third in the process.

00:07:28.759 --> 00:07:31.261
You can see it in the old map

00:07:31.395 --> 00:07:32.329
and calendar.

00:07:32.763 --> 00:07:34.831
Does that world still exist?

00:07:34.965 --> 00:07:36.366
&gt;&gt; I don't know if that world

00:07:36.767 --> 00:07:38.902
still exists, especially the way

00:07:39.036 --> 00:07:39.937
she's prepting herself.

00:07:40.070 --> 00:07:41.305
She's not saying the thing head

00:07:41.438 --> 00:07:41.939
on.

00:07:42.072 --> 00:07:43.941
Even her own question, she faces

00:07:44.074 --> 00:07:45.375
questions because her parents

00:07:45.509 --> 00:07:47.377
are immigrants from far right

00:07:47.511 --> 00:07:48.779
Republicans, how does she plan

00:07:48.779 --> 00:07:51.648
on winning a Republican primary

00:07:51.782 --> 00:07:53.183
talking to the same people that

00:07:53.317 --> 00:07:55.352
she's trying to cater to that

00:07:55.485 --> 00:07:56.920
might be skeptical already of

00:07:57.054 --> 00:07:57.187
her?

00:07:57.321 --> 00:07:58.455
&gt;&gt; A great point.

